!: Kinematic data (2003 nucl. masses)
!: Q-values: -1.644 419 MeV grd. st. -2.073 419 MeV 0.429 MeV level    
!: Ground state threshold:   1.880 768 MeV  up to 1.920 5 MeV double valued
!: first level:
!:      excitation energy       Ethr    Ethr(timrev.)
!:(p,n) 0.429			2.371 496	0.4919
!:
!:(n,p) 0.477612		-	-
!:
!: 20020930: Added ENDF-evaluation (see below) between 7 and 23 MeV. ENDF uses 
!: two more coefficients therefore below and at 7 MeV a compromise between 
!: the Liskien and the ENDF data to get a smoother transition.
!: Data above 23 MeV are 0 deg only, sum of ground AND excited state.
!: 19990708: Included total of 59GI below 1.95 MeV on which LISKIEN depends
!: on. Near threshold energies are about 1.2 keV higher than time-reversed 
!: data of KOEHLER. Included some additional (interpolated) energy points.
!: 19980616: a private communication by DeSimone gives zero-degree values 
!: which are in very good agreement with the predictions of this code 
!: between 2.75 and 3.95 MeV
!: 19971018: energy integrated data of DeSimone et al. (NIM A388,(1997)443) 
!: at zero degree are higher than obtained by the WHIYIE version of this code 
!: (including (p,n1) data) by 5.4% at 2.7 MeV, 2.4% at 3.4 MeV and 3.9% at 
!: 4.1 MeV
!: 19960507 : below 1.95 MeV total from Abramovich et al.
!:   1.8876  4.      1.
!:   1.89   17.35    1.0091 -0.0091
!:  1.89419 16.3987  1.0000  
!: at 1.88695 MeV time reversed data were raised by 6.2%, Abramovich data at
!: 1.89 MeV were lowered by 2%
!: at 1.89419 MeV the integrated time reversed data are 25% lower than 
!: Abramovich
!: 19960414: Integrated near threshold data by time-reversal from 7Be(n,p)7Li
!: (KOEHLER)
!:
!: 95.,27.8,1.   NOT included
!: 135.,23.2,1.  NOT included
!: Status per 19900625: Between 1.95 MeV and 7.00 MeV data from LISKIEN&
!: PAULSEN
!: NOTE: 0 deg. excitation function above 10 MeV are raw data, no smoothing
!: ATTENTION: the code assumes that a given coefficient is zero if at any 
!: higher energy there are no nonzero coefficients of the same or a higher 
!: order!!!
!: If single angle data (e.g. 0 deg, 180 deg) are added to Legendre tables the
!: following steps must be taken:
!1: Add min. energy(EMINL) and maximum energy(EMAXL) of Legendre values in 
!: 1st line
!2: make first added energy value EMAXL+0.1 keV
!3: give AT LEAST 5 additional energy values
